{"type":"text","timestamp":1794359235371,"sessionID":"ses_e37ddf413ffevYpMDlGQN6cfWY","part":{"id":"prt_1c8251314001Dzmb6CkLmgeLij","messageID":"msg_1c824fecf001KfQZAHybhv4M4B","sessionID":"ses_e37ddf413ffevYpMDlGQN6cfWY","type":"text","text":"The lock already has both hashes (line 9-11). So why did pip complain? Because in a constraints file, when using `-c`, pip's `--require-hashes` mode is triggered but it seems to only see one hash. Let me re-read the error more carefully — it says \"their downloaded archives actually had\" with `f4bc...`. That means pip only considered `0ef0...` from the file. Let me check: maybe constraints files with hashes behave differently. Actually the issue is that `-c` (constraints) with hashes — the hashes might be ignored entirely for constraints! Let me test.","time":{"start":1794359235348,"end":1794359235367}}}
