{"type":"text","timestamp":1794359247231,"sessionID":"ses_e37ddf413ffevYpMDlGQN6cfWY","part":{"id":"prt_1c825416b001pM6DG9g7d9bkY2","messageID":"msg_1c8253195001GtsJReFPFV4nb1","sessionID":"ses_e37ddf413ffevYpMDlGQN6cfWY","type":"text","text":"Confirmed: `-c requirements.lock` with hashes triggers `--require-hashes` mode but pip ignores hashes in constraints files, so it fails. This is a bug in the provided scaffold that breaks the Docker build. The README says to update the lock or remove it. \n\nBest fix: make `requirements.lock` a plain constraints file **without** hashes (just pinned versions). That's the standard use of `-c`. Let me regenerate it with pinned versions only. I'll extract the pins from the current lock.","time":{"start":1794359247211,"end":1794359247228}}}
